// RUN: triton-metal-opt --convert-tritongpu-to-metal %s | FileCheck %s
//
// The leet-triton int4 weight-only matmul has two sequential dots per K block:
// even K uses the packed byte's high nibble, odd K uses the low nibble, both
// multiplied by a shared f32 scale. Metal does not generally accept the
// blocked->dot_op layout conversions in that cone, so this exact pattern is
// claimed before the generic convert_layout classifier by a narrow correctness
// fallback op.
//
// CHECK: metal.kernel int4_matmul_kernel
// CHECK: metal.int4_weight_only_matmul
// CHECK-SAME: bm = 64
// CHECK-SAME: bn = 64
// CHECK-SAME: group_size = 32
// CHECK-NOT: tt.dot
// CHECK-NOT: ttg.convert_layout
// CHECK-NOT: scf.for
//
